# L §8.2 One read set (tally 2.1.7 R7, #146; R4's cascade, #143; the review's finding 4, pick P41): "an entry is listed
# under a result exactly when a read in its set gives it". An ask's with pin of r[k1] under an inner as if {r[*] = ...},
# and a with pin of a solve's variable, give no read (the innermost claim wins, L §4.6), so neither is listed; a with
# pin a read takes is (w). refcore 2.1.7 matched the register's text, `r[k1] = ` alone, and listed both.
=== m.tally
model c7
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "invented"
index ks = [k1, k2]
input r[k in ks]: num
input seven: num
input xv: num
input target: num
def tot: num = sum(r[k] for k in ks) at reader
def inner: num = tot as if {r[*] = seven} at reader
def sq: num = xv * xv at reader

ask o3: inner with r[k1] = 9 law 2026-06-30
ask o6: (tot as if {r[*] = seven}) with r[k1] = 9 law 2026-06-30
ask o9: solve sq == target for xv in [0, 4] to 1 with xv = 2 law 2026-06-30
ask w: tot with r[k1] = 9 law 2026-06-30

version v
  cite card
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  r[*] = 1
  seven = 7
  xv = 1
  target = 4
=== expect
o3: 14
  pinned: r[*] = 7
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
o6: 14
  pinned: r[*] = 7
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
o9: 2
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
w: 10
  pinned: r[k1] = 9
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
